The modification is necessary to address the vulnerability CVE-2020-14390, which involves an out-of-bounds memory write that can occur when changing screen size. By deleting the lines:
```
kvfree((void *)softback_buf);
softback_buf = 0UL;
```
we prevent the potential out-of-bounds memory write that could lead to memory corruption or a denial of service. Removing these lines ensures that the vulnerable code related to freeing the softback_buf memory is eliminated, thereby mitigating the risk of exploitation of this vulnerability.

